{
  "key": "pr-1500",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "fix(sm): support label-less issue queries and self-heal stale escalation/park labels",
    "description": "## Summary\n1. **`develop-done` label-less issue search (`githubSource.js`, `smProvider.js`)**: `_issueSearchDescriptors` previously returned `[]` whenever a rule had neither `query.labels` nor `query.assignee`, causing `develop-done` (`mark_developed`) to execute zero searches and never backfill `ai_developed`. Added an `{ kind: 'open' }` descriptor when neither `labels` nor `assignee` is specified in the query (while preserving fail-closed `[]` when `query.assignee` is an unresolvable `{machineAuthor}`).\n2. **Self-clear `rework-loop-escalated` on head move (`reworkLoopGuard.js`, `parkAndActorProbes.js`, `sm_github.json`, `sm_gitlab.json`)**: `park-reset` now also inspects `rework-loop-escalated` PRs and clears the label when the PR head has moved past every recorded `<!-- dmtools:rework-loop-escalated -->` marker head.\n3. **Machine self-unpark when `latestDispatchedVerdict` is `success` (`parkAndActorProbes.js`)**: `evaluateMachineUnpark` now treats `probeHeadVerdictVf() === 'success'` alongside `validationRollupGreen`, so a green dispatched validation run unparks a machine PR even when a skipped merge-bot check keeps the overall check rollup at `pending`."
  }
}

