💡 **SUGGESTION: A machine-created head move (silent-refresh merge) now also clears `rework-loop-escalated`**

The escalation module documents the label as a human handoff: *"The machine stops re-arming while this label stands; a human push (new head) resets the lap budget, and **clearing the label is a human decision**"* (`js/common/reworkLoopGuard.js:47-49`). The new clear path fires on **any** head move — including head moves the machine itself creates:

1. `park-reset` now routes escalated PRs through `update_branch` (`sm_github.json` adds `rework-loop-escalated` to the rule's labels);
2. for a BEHIND escalated PR, the same action's fork-gate silent refresh pushes a machine merge of main (`sm-silent-update` committer) — the head moves;
3. next tick `escalationMovedPastHead` sees the marker head is stale → label cleared → the machine re-arms rework on a PR whose underlying problem (unresolved threads) is untouched → up to `noopLapMax` no-op CI legs before it re-escalates on the new head.

The cycle is bounded (after the merge the PR is no longer BEHIND, so it stabilizes), but it converts a human handoff into 2 wasted CI legs on a head the machine created — the exact burn gh-957 exists to stop. Consider gating the clear on a **substantive** head move: the existing `parkResetCommit` walk (same file, `js/sm/parkAndActorProbes.js:62-77`) already knows how to step past `sm-silent-update`/machine merges to the last substantive commit — requiring that walk to differ from the escalated marker head would keep machine merges from lifting the handoff while preserving the human-push reset this PR wants.

💡 **SUGGESTION: Unpark comment claims "the current head checks are GREEN" when only the dispatched verdict is green**

```javascript
if ( deps.validationRollupGreen(repoInfo, ticket.prNumber) || probeHeadVerdictVf() === 'success' ) {
  return { unpark: true, why: 'the current head checks are GREEN' };
}
```

The new `probeHeadVerdictVf() === 'success'` branch fires precisely when the **rollup is not green** (per the PR description: a skipped `merge / auto-merge` bookkeeping check keeps it `pending`). `unparkWithComment` posts this `why` verbatim to the PR as the unpark audit comment — so on the new branch the posted text can be wrong twice over: it says "checks are GREEN" while the rollup reads `pending`, and if a real non-validation check on the head is red, it claims green while a check is red (the branch only proves the dispatched `quality.yml` run succeeded — `latestDispatchedVerdict` is correctly head-scoped and ignores `cancelled`, `js/sm/mergeAndParkProbes.js:373-384`).

Suggest a distinct `why` for the success branch, e.g. `'the dispatched validation run on the current head concluded success'`, so the PR audit trail states what was actually observed.

